---
// LocalStack · Lesson 2 — S3 CRUD via CLI + first Python/TS SDK side-by-side.
import Lesson from "../../../../layouts/Lesson.astro";
const titlePt = "LocalStack 2 — S3 pelo CLI";
const titleEn = "LocalStack 2 — S3 via the CLI";
const titleFallback = "LocalStack 2 — S3 pelo CLI";
const bodyClass = "lang-pt";
const viewport = "width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0";
const assets = [
	"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../assets/style.css\" />",
	"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../assets/dark.css\" />",
	"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../assets/i18n.css\" />",
	"<script src=\"../assets/i18n.js\" defer></script>",
	"<script src=\"../assets/nav.js\" defer></script>",
	"<script src=\"../assets/reading-ui.js\" defer></script>",
];
---
<Lesson
	titlePt={titlePt}
	titleEn={titleEn}
	titleFallback={titleFallback}
	bodyClass={bodyClass}
	viewport={viewport}
	assets={assets}
>
	<Fragment is:raw>
    <article class="lesson">
      <header class="hero">
        <span class="eyebrow">⬡ LocalStack · Lição 2 · Fácil</span>
        <h1>
          <span data-lang="pt">S3: crie, encha, esvazie, prove</span
          ><span data-lang="en">S3: create, fill, empty, prove</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="lead">
          <span data-lang="pt"
            >O loop completo de S3 no CLI — bucket, upload, listagem,
            download, website — e as <strong>mesmas operações em Python e
            TypeScript</strong>, lado a lado.</span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            >The full S3 loop from the CLI — bucket, upload, listing, download,
            website — plus the <strong>same operations in Python and
            TypeScript</strong>, side by side.</span
          >
        </p>
      </header>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">1</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">O modelo: buckets, chaves e objetos</span
        ><span data-lang="en">The model: buckets, keys and objects</span>
      </h2>
      <p>
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >S3 é um <strong>mapa gigante</strong>: o nome do bucket é o
          namespace, a chave é o caminho do arquivo
          (<code>fotos/gato.jpg</code>), e o valor são os bytes. Não existe
          pasta de verdade — <strong>prefixos simulam pastas</strong>.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >S3 is a <strong>giant map</strong>: the bucket name is the
          namespace, the key is the file path (<code>photos/cat.jpg</code>),
          and the value is the bytes. There are no real folders —
          <strong>prefixes simulate them</strong>.</span
        >
      </p>
      <pre class="block"><code><span class="c"># o vocabulário essencial — decore o verbo, não a flag</span>
awslocal s3 mb s3://meu-bucket            <span class="c"># make bucket</span>
awslocal s3 cp arq.txt s3://meu-bucket/   <span class="c"># upload</span>
awslocal s3 ls s3://meu-bucket             <span class="c"># list</span>
awslocal s3 cp s3://meu-bucket/arq.txt .   <span class="c"># download</span>
awslocal s3 rm s3://meu-bucket/arq.txt     <span class="c"># delete obj</span>
awslocal s3 rb s3://meu-bucket             <span class="c"># remove bucket (vazio)</span></code></pre>
      <div class="callout key">
        <span data-lang="pt"
          ><code>rb</code> se recusa a apagar bucket não-vazio —
          <strong>esvazie antes com <code>awslocal s3 rm s3://b --recursive</code></strong>.
          Isso te protege na AWS real também.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          ><code>rb</code> refuses to delete a non-empty bucket —
          <strong>empty it first with <code>awslocal s3 rm s3://b --recursive</code></strong>.
          That protects you on real AWS too.</span
        >
      </div>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">2</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">Duas linguagens, um cliente: Python + TypeScript</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Two languages, one client: Python + TypeScript</span>
      </h2>
      <p>
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >Regra deste curso: <strong>todo snippet aparece nas duas
          linguagens</strong>. O que muda é a construção do cliente apontando
          para <code>localhost:4566</code>.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >Rule for this course: <strong>every snippet appears in both
          languages</strong>. What changes is building the client pointed at
          <code>localhost:4566</code>.</span
        >
      </p>
      <div class="grid cols-2">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>
            <span data-lang="pt">Python · boto3</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Python · boto3</span>
          </h3>
          <pre class="block"><code>pip install boto3</code></pre>
          <pre class="block"><code><span class="k">import</span> boto3

s3 = boto3.client(
    <span class="s">"s3"</span>,
    endpoint_url=<span class="s">"http://localhost:4566"</span>,
)
s3.create_bucket(Bucket=<span class="s">"py-bucket"</span>)
s3.put_object(
    Bucket=<span class="s">"py-bucket"</span>,
    Key=<span class="s">"hello.txt"</span>,
    Body=<span class="s">"oi do python"</span>.encode(),
)
print(s3.list_objects_v2(
    Bucket=<span class="s">"py-bucket"</span>)\
    [<span class="s">"Contents"</span>][0][<span class="s">"Key"</span>])
<span class="c"># esperado: hello.txt</span></code></pre>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>
            <span data-lang="pt">TypeScript · SDK v3</span
            ><span data-lang="en">TypeScript · SDK v3</span>
          </h3>
          <pre class="block"><code>npm i @aws-sdk/client-s3</code></pre>
          <pre class="block"><code><span class="k">import</span> { S3Client, PutObjectCommand,
  ListObjectsV2Command } <span class="k">from</span> <span class="s">"@aws-sdk/client-s3"</span>;

<span class="k">const</span> s3 = <span class="k">new</span> S3Client({
  endpoint: <span class="s">"http://localhost:4566"</span>,
  region: <span class="s">"us-east-1"</span>,
  credentials: {
    accessKeyId: <span class="s">"test"</span>,
    secretAccessKey: <span class="s">"test"</span>,
  },
});

<span class="k">await</span> s3.send(<span class="k">new</span> PutObjectCommand({
  Bucket: <span class="s">"ts-bucket"</span>,
  Key: <span class="s">"hello.txt"</span>,
  Body: <span class="s">"oi do typescript"</span>,
});
<span class="k">const</span> list = <span class="k">await</span> s3.send(
  <span class="k">new</span> ListObjectsV2Command({
    Bucket: <span class="s">"ts-bucket"</span> }));
console.log(list.Contents![0].Key);
<span class="c">// esperado: hello.txt</span></code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="callout tip">
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >Alternativa sem tocar no código: exporte
          <code>AWS_ENDPOINT_URL=http://localhost:4566</code> — SDKs recentes
          (boto3 e JS v3) honram essa variável.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >Alternative without touching code: export
          <code>AWS_ENDPOINT_URL=http://localhost:4566</code> — recent SDKs
          (boto3 and JS v3) honor that variable.</span
        >
      </div>
      <p class="cite">
        <a href="https://docs.localstack.cloud/aws/services/s3/">S3 no LocalStack</a> ·
        <a href="https://boto3.amazonaws.com/v1/documentation/api/latest/reference/services/s3.html">boto3 · S3</a> ·
        <a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSJavaScriptSDK/v3/latest/client/s3/">SDK v3 · S3</a>
      </p>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">3</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">Desafio (fácil): um site estático em 60 segundos</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Challenge (easy): a static site in 60 seconds</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>
          <span data-lang="pt">Passos</span><span data-lang="en">Steps</span>
        </h3>
        <ol>
          <li>
            <span data-lang="pt">Crie <code>site-patricio</code> e um
            <code>index.html</code> qualquer.</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Create <code>site-patricio</code> and any
            <code>index.html</code>.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span data-lang="pt">Ative o hosting:</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Enable hosting:</span>
            <code>awslocal s3 website s3://site-patricio --index-document index.html</code>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span data-lang="pt">Suba o arquivo e abra o URL abaixo.</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Upload the file and open the URL below.</span>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <pre class="block"><code>mkdir site &amp;&amp; echo <span class="s">"&lt;h1&gt;funcionou&lt;/h1&gt;"</span> &gt; site/index.html
awslocal s3 mb s3://site-patricio
awslocal s3 website s3://site-patricio --index-document index.html
awslocal s3 cp site/index.html s3://site-patricio/index.html
curl http://localhost:4566/site-patricio/index.html
<span class="c"># esperado / expected:</span>
<span class="s">&lt;h1&gt;funcionou&lt;/h1&gt;</span></code></pre>
      <div class="callout warn">
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >Se o <code>curl</code> falhar, use o endpoint alternativo:
          <code>http://s3.localhost.localstack.cloud:4566/site-patricio/index.html</code>
          — <strong>path-style vs virtual-host style</strong> voltará na lição
          de Terraform.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >If the <code>curl</code> fails, use the alternative endpoint:
          <code>http://s3.localhost.localstack.cloud:4566/site-patricio/index.html</code>
          — <strong>path-style vs virtual-host style</strong> returns in the
          Terraform lesson.</span
        >
      </div>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">4</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">Recupere sem pistas</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Retrieve without clues</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="grid cols-2">
        <details class="card">
          <summary>
            <span data-lang="pt">Como apagar um bucket com objetos?</span
            ><span data-lang="en">How to delete a bucket with objects?</span>
          </summary>
          <p><code>awslocal s3 rm s3://b --recursive</code> <span data-lang="pt">e depois</span><span data-lang="en">then</span> <code>awslocal s3 rb s3://b</code></p>
        </details>
        <details class="card">
          <summary>
            <span data-lang="pt">O que é uma "pasta" no S3?</span
            ><span data-lang="en">What is a "folder" in S3?</span>
          </summary>
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt">Um prefixo da chave — nada mais.</span
            ><span data-lang="en">A key prefix — nothing more.</span>
          </p>
        </details>
        <details class="card">
          <summary>
            <span data-lang="pt">Qual parâmetro o boto3 usa para o LocalStack?</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Which parameter does boto3 use for LocalStack?</span>
          </summary>
          <p><code>endpoint_url="http://localhost:4566"</code></p>
        </details>
        <details class="card">
          <summary>
            <span data-lang="pt">E o SDK v3 do TS?</span
            ><span data-lang="en">And the TS SDK v3?</span>
          </summary>
          <p><code>endpoint</code> <span data-lang="pt">no construtor do client</span><span data-lang="en">in the client constructor</span>.</p>
        </details>
      </div>

      <footer class="lesson-foot">
        <div>
          <span data-lang="pt">Fonte primária:</span
          ><span data-lang="en">Primary source:</span>
          <a href="https://docs.localstack.cloud/aws/services/s3/"
            >LocalStack · S3</a
          >
        </div>
        <a class="next-card" href="0003-lambda-python.html"
          ><span class="lbl"
            ><span data-lang="pt">Próxima lição</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Next lesson</span></span
          >
          <div class="t">
            <span data-lang="pt">Lambda em Python — zip, invoke e logs →</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Lambda in Python — zip, invoke and logs →</span>
          </div></a
        >
        <div>
          <span data-lang="pt"
            >Algo não ficou claro? Pergunte ao agente — ele é seu
            professor.</span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            >Anything unclear? Ask the agent—your teacher.</span
          >
          · <a href="../../../index.html">⬡ Hub</a>
        </div>
      </footer>
    </article>
  </Fragment>
</Lesson>
